# --proxy-headers is not optional behind Railway/Render/Fly. slowapi keys rate
# limits on request.client.host, which behind a proxy is the proxy's IP — so
# without it every user on earth shares one 5/minute login bucket, and the first
# person to mistype a password locks out the rest.
#
# --forwarded-allow-ips is the other half: uvicorn ignores X-Forwarded-For unless
# the immediate peer is trusted. '*' is correct only because the platform is the
# only thing that can reach this port; on a host where that is not true, name the
# proxy's IP instead.
web: uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port ${PORT:-8000} --proxy-headers --forwarded-allow-ips='*'
